<section id="how" class="wrap section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL APP. A LONG REACH.</p><h2>Less moving disks.<br>More moving files.</h2></div><p>Keep your favourite computer in the conversation. BitSkim handles the handoff across your local network.</p></div><div class="steps"><article><span class="step-number">01 — FIND</span><h3>Open on both computers.</h3><p>BitSkim discovers nearby computers automatically using broadcasts on your local network. You can also connect by IPv4 address.</p></article><article><span class="step-number">02 — SEND</span><h3>Pick what travels.</h3><p>Choose files or folders. On Mac, drop them straight onto the other computer.</p></article><article><span class="step-number">03 — RECEIVE</span><h3>Give it a home.</h3><p>Accept the offer and choose a destination. Follow the progress or cancel when needed.</p></article></div><p class="security-note">Modern clients prefer TLS encryption. Retro connections use plaintext. Built for a trusted local network. <a href="release-notes.php">Read the details ↗</a></p></section>
